{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Fenwick trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree"],"anchor":"Fenwick-trees"},{"title":"Segment trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree"],"anchor":"Segment-trees"},{"title":"Interval trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree"],"anchor":"Interval-trees"},{"title":"Monoids","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Monoid","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Sum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Product","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Minimum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Maximum","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction"],"anchor":"Monoids"},{"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules","generated":true}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the prefix sums of a sequence of values in one flat array of partial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sums. Prefix sums, range sums and point updates each touch O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") cells, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/FenwickTree\/lowerBound(ofPrefixSum:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" finds where a running total crosses a value by binary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lifting."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import RangeTrees","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","scores.prefixSum(through: 3)        \/\/ 9","scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6)             \/\/ 19","scores.add(10, at: 1)","scores.lowerBound(ofPrefixSum: 15)  \/\/ 2"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Fenwick tree’s update tree, in which each cell’s parent is the next cell an add reaches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one), so Grafluent’s tree algorithms and drawings run over it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" combines any range of values under a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Monoid","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": an associative operation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an identity, written as a type such as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Sum","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Minimum","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or one of your own, which need not be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commutative. Range queries and point updates take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/maxRight(from:where:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/minLeft(upTo:where:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" find how far a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range can grow while a monotone condition on it holds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var heights = SegmentTree<Maximum<Int>>([3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6])","heights.combined(in: 0 ..< 4)        \/\/ 4","heights.update(at: 1, to: 7)","heights.maxRight(from: 0) { $0 < 9 } \/\/ 5"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" also applies an update to every value in a range in O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":"), leaving it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pending at the cells that cover the range. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" names the monoid, the updates and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how an update changes a combined value; it is told how many values the combination covers, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding a constant to a range of sums is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sum + update * count"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree","type":"reference"},{"text":" holds half-open intervals with a value each, in an AVL tree ordered by lower","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound whose vertices also record the largest upper bound below them. It 